<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rivonia Trial</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1963">1963</a>–<a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rivonia Trial was held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a> in 1963–1964 against leaders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-national-congress">African National Congress</a> and its armed wing, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umkhonto-we-sizwe">Umkhonto we Sizwe</a>, after a police raid on their hideout at Liliesleaf Farm in Rivonia, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannesburg">Johannesburg</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a> used his statement from the dock to defend the armed struggle. In June 1964 he and seven others were convicted of sabotage and sentenced to life imprisonment.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rivonia-trial.jpg" alt="Rivonia Trial" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cvanrooyen · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palace_of_Justice,_Church_Square,_pretoria.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…at Liliesleaf Farm in Rivonia in 1963, Mandela, already serving a prison sentence, told the court in the <b>Rivonia Trial</b> that a free and democratic society was “an ideal for which I am prepared to die”; in June 1964 he and seven others were sentenced to life imprisonment.</blockquote><a href="/movement/anti-apartheid-movement">Anti-apartheid movement · Course of Events</a></li><li><blockquote>Mandela and seven co-accused in the <b>Rivonia Trial</b> were sentenced to life for sabotage.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-12">12 June in history</a></li></ul></section>
